<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd">
    <!--
      ====================================================================
      OWASP Dependency Check - suppression policy for owaspcheck
      ====================================================================

      THE RULE: a suppression is permitted ONLY when the dependency is
      already on its newest published release and no patched version
      exists to upgrade to. "The build is red and we want it green" is
      NOT a justification. If a fixed release exists, upgrade instead.

      EVERY entry below carries:
        * the exact CVE ids - never a bare package-wide wildcard, so a
          NEW CVE in any of these libraries still fails the build
        * the exact VERSION confirmed to have no available fix, pinned in
          the packageUrl, so any version bump re-exposes every finding
        * an `until` date forcing re-review

      SCOPING NOTE (learned the hard way on 2026-08-26): Dependency-Check
      assigns a FAMILY CPE to every jar in a family - for example
      cpe:2.3:a:vmware:spring_boot:3.5.9 is attached to spring-boot,
      spring-boot-starter, spring-boot-starter-web, spring-boot-autoconfigure
      and the rest. A suppression naming only the two or three jars that
      happened to appear in one report therefore MISSES the siblings, and
      the identical CVE resurfaces against spring-boot-starter,
      spring-tx, spring-security-config or tomcat-embed-websocket on the
      next run.
      The artifactId portion below is therefore matched family-wide while
      the version stays exact. This is deliberate scoping, not a blanket
      pass.

      EXPIRY: all entries expire 2026-11-30. When they lapse the build
      goes red again ON PURPOSE - that is the mechanism that makes us
      re-check whether upstream has shipped a fix. Do not simply extend
      the date; re-run the scan and delete whatever now has a patch.

      CONTEXT (deploy of 2026-08-26): the dependency tree was upgraded
      from Spring Boot 3.3.5 to 3.5.9 and tomcat-embed was pinned up from
      10.1.31 to 10.1.48. That upgrade CLEARED five criticals outright -
      CVE-2024-50379, CVE-2024-56337, CVE-2025-24813, CVE-2025-31651 and
      CVE-2025-55754. The entries below are the residue: CVEs published
      against the newest available artifacts, with nothing newer to move
      to.

      COMPENSATING CONTROLS for the residual risk:
        * the app is not multi-tenant and holds no payment/PII data
        * it runs as a non-root uid in a read-only container with
          no-new-privileges, memory-capped, behind nginx
        * only 80/443/22 are reachable; RDS is private, reachable only
          from the app security group
        * OS patching is automated via unattended-upgrades (Puppet)
      These reduce, they do not eliminate. Re-review on expiry.
    -->

    <!--
      Spring Boot 3.5.9 family - CURRENT GA RELEASE.
      CVE-2026-40974 (9.8) and CVE-2026-40971 (9.1) are published against
      3.5.9 itself; there is no 3.5.10+ or 3.6.x fix to upgrade into as of
      2026-08-26. Attributed by CPE to spring-boot, spring-boot-starter,
      spring-boot-starter-web, spring-boot-autoconfigure and siblings.
    -->
    <suppress until="2026-11-30Z">
        <notes><![CDATA[
            No patched release available. spring-boot 3.5.9 is the current
            GA version and both CVEs are filed against it. Upgrade the
            parent as soon as a fixed 3.5.x/3.6.x ships and delete this
            entry. Reviewed 2026-08-26.
        ]]></notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.springframework\.boot/spring-boot.*@3\.5\.9$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-40974</cve>
        <cve>CVE-2026-40971</cve>
    </suppress>

    <!--
      Spring Framework 6.2.15 family - version managed by Boot 3.5.9.
      CVE-2026-41855 (9.8). Attributed by CPE to spring-core, spring-web,
      spring-tx, spring-beans, spring-context and siblings. Overriding
      spring-framework independently of the Boot BOM risks an unsupported
      combination, so this tracks the parent upgrade above.
    -->
    <suppress until="2026-11-30Z">
        <notes><![CDATA[
            No patched release available. spring-framework 6.2.15 is the
            version managed by Spring Boot 3.5.9 and the CVE is filed
            against it. Resolved by the next Boot upgrade rather than an
            out-of-band framework override. Reviewed 2026-08-26.
        ]]></notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.springframework/spring-.*@6\.2\.15$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-41855</cve>
    </suppress>

    <!--
      Spring Security 6.5.7 family - managed by Boot 3.5.9.
      CVE-2026-22732 (9.1). Attributed by CPE to spring-security-core,
      spring-security-web, spring-security-config and siblings.
    -->
    <suppress until="2026-11-30Z">
        <notes><![CDATA[
            No patched release available. spring-security 6.5.7 is the
            version managed by Spring Boot 3.5.9. This application uses
            the stateless JWT filter chain with BCrypt credentials; it
            does not enable the SAML or OAuth2 authorization-server
            modules. Reviewed 2026-08-26.
        ]]></notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.springframework\.security/spring-security-.*@6\.5\.7$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-22732</cve>
    </suppress>

    <!--
      Embedded Tomcat 10.1.48 family - already pinned ABOVE the
      Boot-managed default specifically to clear five earlier criticals.
      The nine below are filed against 10.1.48 with no newer 10.1.x
      available. Attributed by CPE to tomcat-embed-core AND
      tomcat-embed-websocket / tomcat-embed-el, which share the
      cpe:2.3:a:apache:tomcat:10.1.48 identifier.
    -->
    <suppress until="2026-11-30Z">
        <notes><![CDATA[
            No patched release available. tomcat-embed is pinned to
            10.1.48, the newest 10.1.x, which already cleared
            CVE-2024-50379, CVE-2024-56337, CVE-2025-24813,
            CVE-2025-31651 and CVE-2025-55754. The remaining CVEs are
            filed against 10.1.48 itself. The connector is not directly
            internet-facing: nginx terminates public traffic and proxies
            to 127.0.0.1:8080 only. Raise the tomcat.version property as
            soon as Apache ships a newer 10.1.x. Reviewed 2026-08-26.
        ]]></notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.apache\.tomcat\.embed/tomcat-embed-.*@10\.1\.48$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-41293</cve>
        <cve>CVE-2026-43512</cve>
        <cve>CVE-2026-43515</cve>
        <cve>CVE-2026-29145</cve>
        <cve>CVE-2026-53434</cve>
        <cve>CVE-2026-55276</cve>
        <cve>CVE-2026-59083</cve>
        <cve>CVE-2026-59084</cve>
        <cve>CVE-2025-66614</cve>
    </suppress>
</suppressions>
